sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  box rgb(254,205,211) People
    actor U as User
  end
  box rgb(191,219,254) Browser
    participant B as Chat page chat.js and socket.js
  end
  box rgb(254,215,170) Moodle
    participant Core as Moodle core login, roles, availability
  end
  box rgb(253,240,138) Moodle plugin local_llmchat
    participant Iss as Token issuer issue_token, scope_builder, jwt
  end
  box rgb(187,247,208) Python server moodle_llm_chat
    participant WS as API websocket endpoint
    participant Ver as API verify_chat_token
    participant DB as Encrypted store
  end

  rect rgba(120,120,140,0.08)
    Note over U,Iss: PHASE 1 - Token generation, inside Moodle
    U->>B: opens the chat page
    B->>Core: AJAX call local_llmchat_issue_token with the course id
    Core->>Core: require login and reject guests
    Core->>Iss: execute, capability local/llmchat:use is required
    Iss->>Core: scope_builder asks which courses and modules this user can see, and their roles
    Core-->>Iss: visible courses, module ids and role archetypes
    Iss->>Iss: add capabilities and the quota claim from site policy and per-user override
    Iss->>Iss: sign HS256 with a key derived by HKDF from the site secret, header kid is the site id, lifetime at most 15 minutes
    Iss-->>B: token, expiry and websocket URL
  end

  rect rgba(120,120,140,0.08)
    Note over B,WS: PHASE 2 - Opening the websocket
    B->>WS: opens wss /ws/chat
    WS->>WS: requires TLS when configured
    B->>WS: first frame must be auth with the token, within 10 seconds
  end

  rect rgba(120,120,140,0.08)
    Note over WS,DB: PHASE 3 - Token verification, inside the Python server
    WS->>Ver: verify_chat_token with consume
    Ver->>Ver: header parses, algorithm is HS256, kid is present
    Ver->>DB: look up the site
    DB-->>Ver: site, rejected if unknown or revoked
    Ver->>DB: list the currently valid secrets, several during a rotation
    Ver->>Ver: derive the key and decode, checking signature, issuer, expiry with 30 s leeway and required claims
    Ver->>Ver: lifetime must not exceed the maximum
    Ver->>DB: consume the jti, a repeated jti is a replay
    Ver->>Ver: build AccessScope, UserProfile and QuotaClaim
    Ver-->>WS: VerifiedToken
    alt token valid
      WS->>WS: Origin must equal the Moodle site origin, at most 3 connections per user
      WS-->>B: ready with tool manifest and user name
      B-->>U: chat is enabled
    else invalid, expired, replayed or wrong origin
      WS-->>B: close with code 4401, 4403 or 4429
    end
  end

  rect rgba(120,120,140,0.08)
    Note over B,Ver: PHASE 4 - Every later message uses a fresh token
    B->>Iss: asks Moodle for a new token before each send, answer or continue
    Iss-->>B: new token with the user's current access
    B->>WS: send frame carrying the new token
    WS->>Ver: verify_chat_token with consume
    Ver-->>WS: VerifiedToken, so a changed enrolment applies within one turn
  end
